## The Challenge

### An Ayurvedic brand that didn't want to look Ayurvedic.

The Ayurvedic beauty market is full of brands that look exactly the same — earthy greens, busy botanical prints, and labels packed with Sanskrit. The Immuno Co. wanted none of that. They were building something new: Ayurveda that feels modern, premium, and genuinely approachable to a younger buyer.

The ask was clear: minimalist, pastel, and different. A product range that needed to work across two distinct lines — Herb Enriched hair care and Skin Brightening skincare — while still looking like it all belongs to the same family. Clean. Confident. Nothing gaudy.

The brief was tight. But somewhere along the way, the project became a lot bigger than just packaging.

### "Minimalist, not gaudy. Different, but not trying too hard. That's a short brief with a big ask behind it."

## Our Process

### Five phases. One shared direction throughout.

### 01 Discovery

Brief deep-dive, competitor audit, audience mapping

### 02 Moodboard

Color direction, texture references, packaging inspiration

### 03 Illustration

Sketches → AI exploration → final Illustrator artwork

### 04 Color Proofing

Physical prints reviewed together until the color was right

### 05 Delivery

Print-ready files, 3D visuals, Amazon A+ content

