## The results

### Packaging that people actually noticed.

The Immuno Co. launched on Amazon with a full product range — seven SKUs, two product lines, every file print-ready and delivered on time. But what happened after launch is what makes this one worth talking about.

The packaging became the most commented-on thing about the brand. Customers on Amazon started calling out the design in their reviews — the look, the feel, how different it seemed from everything else in the Ayurvedic category. For a new brand in a crowded space, that kind of organic recognition is exactly what you want in the early days.

Sales picked up. Repeat orders followed. And the brand that launched with a brief about being "different" was starting to genuinely stand out — not just on a slide deck, but on a screen where real people were buying.

### 01. Customers noticed the packaging in reviews

Organic mentions of the design on Amazon from real buyers, without being prompted.

### 02. Sales grew after launch

Repeat orders started coming in as the brand found its footing on the platform.

### 03. Stood out in a crowded category

In a sea of similar Ayurvedic brands, the visual identity gave The Immuno Co. a clear identity of its own.

